WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.130
A freezing bus stop.

2
00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:05.590
Your phone rings, and you tap
to answer with your gloves on.

3
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:06.550
Nothing.

4
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.710
Tap again.

5
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:08.850
Still nothing.

6
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.350
Glove off, one tap, and
it answers straight away.

7
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.730
Later, same gloves, at
a self-service kiosk.

8
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.450
You touch the screen, and this one works.

9
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.470
So what can your finger
do that your glove can't?

10
00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.330
Is your phone feeling
the warmth of your skin?

11
00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:28.470
In this mission, you'll see how input
devices turn real-world actions,

12
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:30.750
like a key press, into data.

13
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.270
You'll find there's more than
one kind of touch screen,

14
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:35.810
and they detect a touch in different ways.

15
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:40.640
Your mission: explain why your phone screen
feels your finger but not your glove.
